The legal text is the Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia (Undang-Undang Dasar Negara Republik
Indonesia Tahun 1945), as published by Mahkamah Konstitusi Republik Indonesia (Constitutional Court) in
"Buku Saku UUD 1945 dan UU MK" (2020), https://pusdik.mkri.id, retrieved 29 October 2026.
The publication states no reuse licence. Attribution: Mahkamah Konstitusi Republik Indonesia.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text layer of the PDF was converted to one Markdown file per article,
one paragraph or item per line; page numbers, chapter headings, footnote keys and amendment asterisks
were removed; line wraps were joined. The wording of the law was not changed. The Constitutional Court
does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

Penal Code (Kitab Undang-Undang Hukum Pidana, Undang-Undang Nomor 1 Tahun 2023): text recognised by OCR from the
signed copy ("salinan") published by Peraturan BPK (JDIH BPK), https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Download/287456,
retrieved 30 October 2026. Statutes are not protected by copyright in Indonesia. Undang-Undang Nomor 28 Tahun
2014 tentang Hak Cipta, Pasal 42: "Tidak ada Hak Cipta atas hasil karya berupa: a. hasil rapat terbuka lembaga
negara; b. peraturan perundang-undangan; c. pidato kenegaraan atau pidato pejabat pemerintah; d. putusan
pengadilan atau penetapan hakim; dan e. kitab suci atau simbol keagamaan." Attribution: Badan Pemeriksa
Keuangan (BPK) / Sekretariat Negara. Changes made by Lexifina: OCR, then removal of page headers, footers and
catchwords, joining of wrapped lines, restoration of list punctuation, and the hand corrections named in the
README. The wording of the law was not otherwise changed.
